{"id": "0f2cb788-2440-468d-a88a-8dd91c2d82af", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The timeout started at 19:36:30 and runs 72 hours, ending 2026-11-21 19:36:30 — so from now at 21:24 I'm looking at roughly a 1h48m wait. I also note the approver is the Admin IAM role, so sessions assumed from that role should count as valid approvers.

Since the executor is also an assumed-role session under Admin, self-approval doesn't appear to be blocked by this runbook, though I shouldn't assert that definitively. The executor would also need the ssm:SendAutomationSignal permission, and I should note the DevOps Agent role itself can't approve.

"}]}
